
%9Syntax:%9

TK %|[-server <tag>] [-mask ident|host|domain] [-force] [-dry] <nick|user@host> [<time>] <reason>
TK HELP%|
TK MASK %|[-server <tag>] [-mask ident|host|domain] <nick>
TK PENDING%|
TK RECENT%|
TK YES%|
TK NO%|
TK LIST %|[<mask>]
TK KLIST %|[<mask>]

%9Parameters:%9

    HELP:        Short built-in help of the script (same as /TKHELP), with
                 the list of settings and the audit log path.
    MASK:        Runs WHOIS on the nick and shows its ident@host and the
                 masks the script would build (ident, host, domain). Sends
                 nothing and does not require IRC operator status.
    PENDING:     Requests waiting for a WHOIS reply, with waiting time.
    RECENT:      The last 20 TKLINE/UNTKLINE commands sent in this
                 session: time, tag, mask, duration and reason.
    YES:         Sends the TKLINE waiting for confirmation (tk_confirm).
    NO:          Cancels the TKLINE waiting for confirmation.
    LIST:        Same as /TKLIST (STATS k).
    KLIST:       Same as /KLIST (STATS K).

    Without a subcommand /TK works exactly like /TKL and takes the same
    options and arguments.

%9Description:%9

    The main command of the tk.pl script - temporary K-lines (TKLINE) for
    ircd 2.11 (IRCnet). See /HELP TKL for how K-lines are set.

    Confirmations (tk_confirm = ON) are kept separately for each server:
    YES and NO apply to the server of the active window, and at most one
    TKLINE waits per server - a new one replaces the previous one. After
    60 seconds YES replies "nothing to confirm".

    A nick that equals a subcommand name (e.g. "yes", "list") must be
    given with /TKL - /TK would treat it as the subcommand.

%9Settings:%9

    tk_mask_type = ident
        Default mask type: ident, host or domain.
    tk_default_time = 30m
        K-line duration when none is given in the command.
    tk_max_time = 30d
        Longest allowed duration; 0 or empty = no limit.
    tk_whois_timeout_ms = 10000
        How long to wait for WHOIS (clamped to 2000-60000 ms).
    tk_reason_max = 0
        Maximum reason length; 0 = the server's TOPICLEN, or 160 without it.
    tk_require_oper = ON
        Without +o (/OPER) the TKL and UNTKL commands refuse to work.
    tk_allow_broad = OFF
        ON allows broad masks without -force.
    tk_confirm = OFF
        ON = every TKLINE requires confirmation with /TK YES.
    tk_audit = ON
        Log events to ~/.erssi/tk_audit.jsonl (JSON, mode 0600).

%9Examples:%9

    /TK spammer 30m advertising flood
    /TK MASK spammer
    /TK -mask host -dry spammer 1h clones
    /TK YES
    /TK RECENT

%9See also:%9 KLIST, TKHELP, TKL, TKLIST, UNTKL

